            <div xml:id="d492">

                <pb facs="0562" n="544" sameAs="frus:frus1946v11/pg544"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">832.6363/5–1446: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in Brazil</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Daniels</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left"><hi rendition="#small-caps">confidential</hi></seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Rio de
                                janeiro</hi></placeName> [<date
                            ana="#date_undated-inferred-from-document-content" calendar="gregorian"
                            notAfter="1946-05-14T19:50:00-04:00"
                            notBefore="1946-05-14T17:00:00-04:00" when="1946-05-14"
                        >undated</date>.]<lb/>[Received May 14, 1946—7:50 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>896. ReEmbstel 894, May 14, 5 p.m.<anchor n="85" xml:id="d492-f1"/> This
                    afternoon when presenting Admiral Bieri to President Dutra latter spoke to me
                    aside <pb facs="0563" n="545" xml:id="pg545"/> and said he had read the
                    memorandum on petroleum policy I handed Gracie yesterday afternoon. Dutra
                    expressed satisfaction with memorandum and added that he expected no
                    unsurmountable difficulty in obtaining desired revision Brazilian legislative
                    provisions permitting foreign capital participation.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Daniels</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
